WEBVTT

01:04.147 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:08.943 --> 01:12.322
Now we have a house

01:13.490 --> 01:14.908
and a boat.

01:16.618 --> 01:18.328
This is crazy.

01:20.330 --> 01:21.164
Are you happy?

01:21.247 --> 01:22.082
Yeah.

01:24.501 --> 01:25.877
I'm so happy.

01:37.430 --> 01:38.348
Stop it.

01:49.275 --> 01:52.487
It was the brightest season
that would never return.

01:55.198 --> 01:59.369
LIFE GOES ON AND ON

02:23.560 --> 02:25.979
HALLIM DISASTER RELIEF
DEPUTY CHIEF OH AE-SUN

02:33.611 --> 02:35.321
BABY FORMULA

02:47.417 --> 02:50.295
I have to live up to my title, right?

02:56.759 --> 02:58.761
I'm the deputy chief, after all.

02:59.345 --> 03:01.723
Let's add two more. I'm the deputy chief.

03:19.115 --> 03:21.534
Seriously, you little troublemaker!

03:22.410 --> 03:25.997
I told you I'd give you candy
after you finish your sujebi, didn't I?

03:26.873 --> 03:29.459
Why don't you ever listen to Mommy?

03:29.542 --> 03:33.421
Mommy, give me a hug.

03:34.214 --> 03:37.300
Mommy, give me a hug.

03:37.383 --> 03:40.762
Mommy, give me a hug.

03:40.845 --> 03:43.556
Ms. Oh! Geum-myeong was in an accident!

03:44.140 --> 03:45.099
-Mommy.
-What?

03:45.183 --> 03:46.476
Mommy.

03:49.354 --> 03:51.314
Is she bleeding?

03:52.023 --> 03:53.441
I don't know. It's that way.

03:55.693 --> 03:59.489
Auntie! Please watch my kids, okay?

04:33.606 --> 04:35.525
Are you the Dragon King's daughter?

04:36.025 --> 04:39.904
Wild dolphins mean a storm is coming,
and you're riding your bike?

04:40.822 --> 04:43.366
The motorcycle hit me. I didn't hit it.

04:44.784 --> 04:47.203
Jeju's winds can flip cars, you know?

04:47.287 --> 04:49.872
This tiny thing would be flipped
a hundred times.

04:59.382 --> 05:00.216
Auntie!

05:02.635 --> 05:03.553
Auntie!

05:09.058 --> 05:10.226
Auntie!

05:11.436 --> 05:12.603
What about my kids?

05:15.273 --> 05:16.607
Did you put them to bed?

05:16.691 --> 05:18.526
Come again? Which kids?

05:28.244 --> 05:29.078
Eun-myeong!

05:30.913 --> 05:32.874
Why did you leave the boys alone?

05:33.458 --> 05:34.876
It wasn't even a big accident.

05:34.959 --> 05:36.461
-Eun-myeong.
-Eun-myeong!

05:36.544 --> 05:37.462
Baby!

05:37.545 --> 05:39.380
-Dong-myeong!
-Eun-myeong! Dong-myeong!

05:39.464 --> 05:40.715
-Dong-myeong!
-Baby!

05:41.424 --> 05:42.425
Baby!

05:42.508 --> 05:43.343
Eun-myeong!

05:44.093 --> 05:45.928
Eun-myeong!

05:47.096 --> 05:48.598
Eun-myeong…

05:56.356 --> 05:58.524
Grandma always said
once boys start running,

05:58.608 --> 06:00.401
they'll go everywhere!

06:00.485 --> 06:02.320
-Remember?
-Their shoes.

06:03.654 --> 06:04.697
They aren't here.

06:07.742 --> 06:09.494
I'll go to the cabbage field.

06:09.577 --> 06:12.455
-Ae-sun! Pay me for my green laver.
-You can keep looking.

06:13.289 --> 06:15.625
I had to bring your eldest son,

06:16.501 --> 06:18.878
so I missed out on harvesting the laver.

06:18.961 --> 06:20.838
You're driving me crazy.

06:22.423 --> 06:25.051
Didn't I tell you to stay in the house?

06:25.718 --> 06:29.889
He was standing alone
on the seawall looking for you.

06:31.057 --> 06:34.018
What were you thinking,
going there on your own?

06:34.102 --> 06:38.481
The truck auntie would have come for you.
Why couldn't you just wait and…

06:39.232 --> 06:42.735
If you stand there,
the waves will swallow you up.

06:42.819 --> 06:46.697
Even cows are swept away by Jeju typhoons.
You must be careful!

06:47.949 --> 06:48.783
And Dong-myeong?

06:52.662 --> 06:55.206
-Where is Dong-myeong?
-At home.

06:55.957 --> 06:58.251
Wasn't Dong-myeong with you?

07:00.420 --> 07:01.462
At home!

07:04.173 --> 07:08.010
What are you saying? You're scaring me!

07:08.094 --> 07:11.764
Mommy, give me a hug.

07:11.848 --> 07:14.976
-Is she bleeding?
-Mommy.

07:49.302 --> 07:50.344
Geum-myeong,

07:51.387 --> 07:53.222
call the fishing co-op office.

08:04.942 --> 08:06.903
Who can stop the summer's whims?

08:07.653 --> 08:11.032
Just yesterday, it was bright and sunny
like a newlywed bride.

08:11.699 --> 08:15.161
Then it suddenly turns aggressive,
like a wife losing her temper.

08:15.244 --> 08:19.499
A wife you can replace,
but you can't hide from the summer frenzy.

08:21.250 --> 08:22.084
For God's sake.

08:22.793 --> 08:23.711
Crap!

08:25.171 --> 08:26.088
Good God.

08:26.714 --> 08:28.758
He's building a retaining wall
with his mouth.

08:30.051 --> 08:32.929
Gwan-sik!

08:39.602 --> 08:41.771
Baby! Dong-myeong!

08:42.438 --> 08:43.314
Dong-myeong!

08:45.775 --> 08:46.651
Dong-myeong!

08:47.318 --> 08:48.736
Dong-myeong!

08:49.695 --> 08:53.282
-Yang Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

08:53.366 --> 08:54.575
Dong-myeong!

08:56.327 --> 08:58.538
Dong-myeong!

08:58.621 --> 08:59.664
Yang Dong-myeong!

09:00.373 --> 09:01.624
Dong-myeong!

09:03.209 --> 09:05.378
Dong-myeong!

09:07.713 --> 09:10.925
-Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

09:11.676 --> 09:13.594
-Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

09:13.678 --> 09:15.263
-Yang Dong-myeong!
-Dong-myeong!

09:15.346 --> 09:18.808
Where did he go? Dong-myeong!

09:20.101 --> 09:21.811
Dong-myeong!

09:23.062 --> 09:25.147
Dong-myeong! Baby!

09:27.358 --> 09:29.819
Yang Dong-myeong! Baby!

09:31.237 --> 09:32.238
Dong-myeong!

09:34.532 --> 09:35.866
Yang Dong-myeong!

09:35.950 --> 09:39.912
Please have mercy on us.
Whatever it takes, spare the child.

09:39.996 --> 09:42.999
Please spare our baby.
Send him back to us.

09:43.916 --> 09:45.668
Please send our baby back to us.

09:50.423 --> 09:52.550
Losing a child takes
only a moment's lapse.

09:52.633 --> 09:54.176
Please save my grandson.

09:54.260 --> 09:56.679
Do you know
what everyone in the world says

09:57.346 --> 09:59.223
when they lose their children?

10:00.057 --> 10:02.393
-Dong-myeong. My baby.
-They all say the same thing.

10:02.476 --> 10:04.854
They say it happens
in the blink of an eye.

10:04.937 --> 10:07.607
They lost their child
in the blink of an eye!

10:14.238 --> 10:15.698
Did you find him? Did they?

10:17.033 --> 10:19.327
-Ae-sun.
-Did you find him?

10:22.038 --> 10:22.955
Ae-sun.

10:28.336 --> 10:29.211
Ae-sun.

10:30.630 --> 10:31.756
What?

10:32.757 --> 10:33.716
What?

11:06.207 --> 11:07.208
Hospital.

11:08.584 --> 11:10.461
We need to go to the hospital.

11:11.837 --> 11:12.672
Oh dear.

11:14.131 --> 11:15.758
My baby's cold.

11:19.053 --> 11:21.847
Why won't anyone call an ambulance?

11:26.769 --> 11:27.603
Dong-myeong.

11:28.354 --> 11:29.188
Baby.

11:29.814 --> 11:30.648
Baby.

11:31.357 --> 11:32.191
Dong-myeong.

11:33.984 --> 11:34.902
Dong-myeong.

11:35.736 --> 11:36.612
Baby.

11:37.571 --> 11:38.406
Baby.

11:39.115 --> 11:40.491
What's wrong with him?

11:42.201 --> 11:43.202
Baby.

11:45.538 --> 11:46.580
The doctor.

11:48.374 --> 11:50.626
We need to call the doctor.

12:03.347 --> 12:06.183
Gwan-sik, call an ambulance.

12:07.017 --> 12:10.312
Why won't anyone call an ambulance?

12:11.772 --> 12:13.733
No one's calling an ambulance.

12:18.988 --> 12:20.740
On the day their world collapsed…

12:31.459 --> 12:32.752
for the first time…

12:36.464 --> 12:38.174
their Steelheart collapsed.

13:39.193 --> 13:42.780
A father's weeping drowned out the waves.

15:07.406 --> 15:09.491
I should've hugged him.

15:14.330 --> 15:16.165
I should've hugged him.

15:18.292 --> 15:20.294
The son she had fed lunch

15:21.629 --> 15:23.631
was no longer the same by dinner.

15:25.049 --> 15:29.762
Mommy, give me a hug.

15:30.387 --> 15:31.805
Mommy, give me a hug.

15:32.389 --> 15:33.974
Mommy, give me a hug.

15:34.516 --> 15:36.393
Mommy, give me a hug.

15:36.477 --> 15:39.188
Mommy, give me a hug.

15:47.947 --> 15:49.865
I should've hugged him while I could.

15:54.203 --> 15:55.412
I should've…

16:14.890 --> 16:19.770
Grandma didn't utter a word of blame
toward Mom during the funeral.

16:21.271 --> 16:25.234
She said a mother who has lost her child
sheds more tears than the sea.

16:37.871 --> 16:38.706
Keep living.

16:40.207 --> 16:41.834
What choice do you have?

16:42.876 --> 16:46.171
You have two children
who still need to be fed.

16:49.717 --> 16:51.802
Life will go on if you keep living.

16:52.302 --> 16:53.762
Life will go on and on.

16:56.056 --> 16:57.474
Life goes on and on.

16:58.183 --> 17:00.602
There will be tougher days in your life.

17:01.854 --> 17:06.358
One day, life might get so tough
that you feel like you can't go on--

17:06.442 --> 17:08.027
I told you to stop talking!

17:08.652 --> 17:10.112
I won't promise.

17:10.821 --> 17:12.781
I'm not going to eat abalone.

17:17.327 --> 17:18.454
My precious little one.

17:20.664 --> 17:21.999
When will you grow up?

17:33.093 --> 17:33.927
Ae-sun.

17:34.720 --> 17:37.598
If life gets so tough
that you feel like you can't go on,

17:37.681 --> 17:39.558
remember me, who dived every day.

17:43.353 --> 17:48.108
Those who make a living on land
mention dying over the slightest hardship.

17:49.610 --> 17:51.361
But no matter how tough life gets,

17:52.112 --> 17:54.156
a haenyeo would never say that.

17:55.908 --> 17:59.870
I've come close to death countless time
in those fierce waters, and each time,

18:01.121 --> 18:03.207
I found countless reasons to keep living.

18:03.290 --> 18:04.666
Then keep living.

18:05.542 --> 18:06.710
You should live on.

18:07.211 --> 18:09.546
Why die with countless reasons to live?

18:13.092 --> 18:15.803
Your mind can't weep
if your body is weary.

18:16.595 --> 18:20.599
One day, life might get so tough
that you feel like you can't go on.

18:21.266 --> 18:22.518
Don't just lie still.

18:23.310 --> 18:24.770
Struggle with all your might.

18:25.354 --> 18:26.814
Stomp wash your blanket.

18:27.314 --> 18:30.192
Plow the field or even do odd jobs
to earn some money.

18:30.275 --> 18:34.154
Tell yourself you won't die
and must survive, no matter what.

18:35.030 --> 18:36.907
Paddle your arms and legs like crazy.

18:39.034 --> 18:41.537
You'll get through the dark waters

18:43.163 --> 18:44.498
and see the sky.

18:47.835 --> 18:49.753
You'll be able to breathe again.

19:15.070 --> 19:16.071
You can do it?

19:17.906 --> 19:19.074
It'd be sweet, right?

19:26.623 --> 19:28.041
That looks so good.

19:40.721 --> 19:42.598
Is that what you wanted to eat?

19:45.642 --> 19:48.020
Is that what you've been craving?

19:52.482 --> 19:54.568
Why won't you talk to me?

19:56.528 --> 19:57.905
Are you mad at Mommy?

20:43.659 --> 20:44.952
Yang Eun-myeong.

20:45.577 --> 20:47.871
I asked why you won't talk to me.

20:51.625 --> 20:53.168
Are you never gonna talk to me again?

21:27.995 --> 21:31.790
SCHOOL SUPPORT FEES DUE BY THE 20TH

21:47.681 --> 21:49.766
Why didn't you show us the perfect score?

21:51.310 --> 21:53.103
Why didn't you show them off to me?

22:00.110 --> 22:00.986
Geum-myeong.

22:04.698 --> 22:05.532
What's wrong?

22:06.408 --> 22:07.701
Are you mad at Mommy?

22:08.327 --> 22:10.329
You won't talk because you're mad at me?

22:11.872 --> 22:12.748
Is it because…

22:14.958 --> 22:15.792
Is it because…

22:19.671 --> 22:21.340
I didn't bring your brother back?

22:22.966 --> 22:25.260
Are you not talking to me
because you're mad at me?

22:27.512 --> 22:29.139
Because you're angry.

22:32.392 --> 22:33.393
What was that?

22:34.269 --> 22:36.605
I left my brother behind.

22:37.606 --> 22:38.982
That's why he's dead.

22:48.533 --> 22:49.368
It's because…

22:51.036 --> 22:51.995
It's because…

22:53.080 --> 22:54.623
I went to ride my bike.

22:56.041 --> 22:59.586
If I hadn't gone to ride my bike,
Dong-myeong would still be alive.

23:00.087 --> 23:01.088
I was told…

23:03.048 --> 23:05.342
not to ride my bike
because of the typhoon,

23:06.510 --> 23:10.263
but I still went to ride it.

23:10.347 --> 23:12.474
That's why Dong-myeong is dead.

23:17.729 --> 23:18.897
Mom and Dad said

23:20.315 --> 23:24.236
that was when they came to their senses.

23:28.949 --> 23:30.450
I'm sorry.

23:31.618 --> 23:32.494
I'm so sorry.

23:34.037 --> 23:34.871
I'm sorry.

23:36.248 --> 23:37.541
It's all my fault.

23:38.458 --> 23:39.793
I'm sorry, Eun-myeong.

24:14.911 --> 24:17.747
The Steelheart picked himself up
after three days.

24:18.498 --> 24:20.542
He finished his mountain of rice

24:21.710 --> 24:23.545
and then simply went out to sea.

24:38.268 --> 24:39.102
Geum-myeong,

24:39.686 --> 24:41.354
tell your teacher

24:41.438 --> 24:44.858
Dad will pay the school support fees
in three days.

24:50.405 --> 24:51.281
Okay?

24:53.909 --> 24:57.037
They were allowed three days to mourn.

24:58.788 --> 25:00.248
Just three days.

25:04.586 --> 25:08.048
Dad, what will you catch today?

25:08.715 --> 25:11.343
Brown croakers. Summer brown croakers.

25:12.594 --> 25:14.012
-Brown croakers?
-Yes.

25:14.930 --> 25:17.557
I won't sell them. I'll bring them home.

25:18.141 --> 25:19.476
-Our home?
-Yeah.

25:21.186 --> 25:24.022
Let's have them for dinner tonight.

25:25.440 --> 25:26.942
Let's eat together.

26:20.704 --> 26:21.997
You're not eating?

26:22.497 --> 26:24.624
She sold everything and is packing up now.

26:25.500 --> 26:29.421
She has her back to the sea,
but she still sells well, right?

26:30.714 --> 26:34.009
She can't even stand the sight
of that damn sea.

26:35.677 --> 26:37.429
But just how clear is that sea?

26:38.513 --> 26:42.142
It looks so clear and peaceful,
as if nothing happened,

26:42.225 --> 26:44.144
that it makes her want to vomit.

26:48.440 --> 26:52.694
The sea took her mother,
her father, and now her son.

26:52.777 --> 26:56.114
Imagine how she feels
having to make a living from that sea.

26:57.699 --> 27:01.494
She's enduring life with a heart
crudely stitched back together.

27:02.954 --> 27:05.498
The Dragon King sure is fickle, isn't he?

27:05.999 --> 27:08.251
He's taken everything she holds dear,

27:08.960 --> 27:13.965
yet he keeps giving her things
as if to say, "I still won't let you die."

27:14.841 --> 27:16.635
I'm grateful to that little one.

27:17.427 --> 27:19.179
I'm grateful she's carrying on.

27:20.680 --> 27:22.599
Did you sell all the squid?

27:23.224 --> 27:25.602
I managed to catch
a longtooth grouper today.

27:26.353 --> 27:29.981
If we sell it,
we could easily make 1,000 won.

27:34.986 --> 27:37.489
More than enough
to buy Eun-myeong a new backpack.

27:37.989 --> 27:39.532
It's so unfair.

27:45.205 --> 27:46.623
It's all so unfair.

27:55.423 --> 27:57.300
Geum-myeong. Eun-myeong. Let's go.

28:14.442 --> 28:16.027
I really don't want

28:17.737 --> 28:19.906
anything to do with that damn sea.

28:22.826 --> 28:24.369
It's so unfair.

28:27.914 --> 28:28.748
Ae-sun.

28:30.625 --> 28:31.835
Let's stop crying.

28:34.337 --> 28:38.258
If Mom and Dad keep crying,
it will cast a shadow over the children.

28:39.134 --> 28:40.218
They'll be anxious.

28:41.261 --> 28:44.180
I just want this damn summer to be over.

28:46.099 --> 28:48.226
It's so annoying how fickle it is.

28:49.686 --> 28:51.479
When it's bright, it's too bright.

28:52.480 --> 28:53.940
When it rains, it pours.

28:55.942 --> 28:58.653
Summer allows everything on land
and at sea to thrive,

28:59.237 --> 29:01.406
and then it brings storms that crush them.

29:01.906 --> 29:03.283
We're completely helpless.

29:04.075 --> 29:05.702
The two-faced summer

29:06.327 --> 29:10.039
brought my young parents to their knees.

29:10.707 --> 29:13.293
Why does it have to be so harsh?

29:14.711 --> 29:16.504
If it were me, I'd go easy.

29:19.924 --> 29:22.135
Even drivers cut beginners some slack.

29:24.471 --> 29:26.139
Everything is a first for me too.

29:28.641 --> 29:30.518
Why can't it go easy on me?

29:32.103 --> 29:34.272
Like the grass flattened by a typhoon…

29:35.648 --> 29:37.567
How can we move on from this?

29:38.568 --> 29:41.404
…they fell down but got back up again.

29:41.488 --> 29:45.533
Still, the summer's fickleness
will help us go on.

29:48.411 --> 29:51.831
Grass and trees knocked down
by the summer typhoon

29:52.415 --> 29:53.750
eventually rise again.

29:56.336 --> 29:59.130
Rain may pour
as if it would sweep everything away.

30:01.007 --> 30:05.553
But once the sun starts blazing again,
life rises again, no matter what.

30:06.387 --> 30:08.181
Everything on land and at sea.

30:12.393 --> 30:13.770
What if I can't go on?

30:16.689 --> 30:19.859
I keep thinking I can't go on.

30:23.112 --> 30:24.656
-There are crabs here.
-Crabs?

30:24.739 --> 30:26.241
We have to save the kids.

30:27.200 --> 30:28.284
You can't catch that.

30:35.041 --> 30:36.251
Gwan-sik.

30:42.757 --> 30:44.676
It was my fault.

30:46.177 --> 30:48.137
I was the one…

30:51.891 --> 30:53.852
who'd put Dong-myeong on the seawall.

31:03.987 --> 31:09.158
Ever since he turned one,
I'd carry him to greet you on the seawall.

31:12.203 --> 31:14.581
I'd line the kids up and tell them,

31:16.416 --> 31:18.418
"If we stand here, Dad will come."

31:23.256 --> 31:25.675
I told them
that even if there was rain or wind,

31:27.427 --> 31:30.138
you'd come back to us if we waited there.

31:39.856 --> 31:40.982
I told them that.

31:45.528 --> 31:47.030
Our Dong-myeong…

31:51.868 --> 31:53.494
died because of me.

32:00.752 --> 32:02.170
It was all my fault.

32:08.718 --> 32:11.554
The heavens and the Dragon King are harsh.
They're to blame.

32:17.644 --> 32:19.187
It's not your fault at all.

32:19.812 --> 32:20.688
Okay?

32:22.649 --> 32:25.193
No one in our family is to blame.
No one at all.

32:27.153 --> 32:32.158
Dad kept telling himself that,
but deep down, he did resent someone.

32:34.452 --> 32:40.166
Mom said she found out
who he resented 30 years later.

32:48.383 --> 32:49.550
Hey.

32:49.634 --> 32:51.010
ENDOSCOPY CENTER

32:51.094 --> 32:54.305
Do you know what your dad muttered?

32:57.475 --> 32:58.977
Did he speak gibberish?

32:59.686 --> 33:01.604
People do that during endoscopies.

33:08.361 --> 33:10.238
What, did he mention another woman?

33:15.326 --> 33:16.285
Retaining wall.

33:17.578 --> 33:18.955
What? "Retaining wall"?

33:19.998 --> 33:20.832
Gwan-sik!

33:21.666 --> 33:22.500
Gwan-sik!

33:22.583 --> 33:25.920
"I shouldn't have gone
to build the retaining wall."

33:27.630 --> 33:29.465
"I shouldn't have gone."

33:31.092 --> 33:32.301
That's what he said.

33:36.848 --> 33:39.225
No one else has a heart of steel like him.

33:39.892 --> 33:42.353
Once something enters him,
it will never escape.

33:42.937 --> 33:44.647
He keeps it all bottled up inside.

33:45.982 --> 33:47.650
I don't know how he keeps going.

33:48.735 --> 33:50.486
How did you both keep going?

33:54.574 --> 33:55.950
What, then? Give up?

33:56.743 --> 34:01.539
We still had two kids
with twinkling eyes watching us.

34:04.542 --> 34:06.377
I guess we saved you and Dad.

34:07.503 --> 34:09.005
Of course you did.

34:10.214 --> 34:11.841
You saved us.

34:17.388 --> 34:19.223
If it weren't for you…

34:20.266 --> 34:22.101
If it weren't for you guys…

34:23.269 --> 34:26.647
NAME OF THE DECEASED: YANG DONG-MYEONG

34:35.281 --> 34:37.909
HEAD OF HOUSEHOLD: YANG GWAN-SIK

34:37.992 --> 34:41.579
RELATIONSHIP TO HEAD OF HOUSEHOLD: SON

34:46.459 --> 34:49.879
DATE OF BIRTH: SEPTEMBER 6, 1974

34:54.342 --> 34:59.055
3 YEARS OLD

35:21.577 --> 35:24.747
No words can describe
the pain of losing your child.

35:29.961 --> 35:32.380
He couldn't even cry openly anywhere.

35:33.297 --> 35:36.342
His heart was completely shattered.

35:50.398 --> 35:52.733
You can't eat dalgona as a meal.

35:55.778 --> 35:57.572
I already finished all my food.

35:58.281 --> 35:59.949
Right. Stop eating.

36:07.623 --> 36:11.002
I wondered how we'd ever go on.

36:12.295 --> 36:14.881
What could you possibly have eaten?

36:18.551 --> 36:20.469
I eat every day.

36:20.970 --> 36:22.763
They usually bring meat too.

36:31.981 --> 36:37.528
We were able to go on
thanks to the people who fed us.

36:40.531 --> 36:42.700
A canola flower never blooms alone.

36:42.783 --> 36:44.493
They bloom in a bunch.

36:45.786 --> 36:49.165
If I had been alone,
I would have broken down countless times.

36:54.629 --> 36:57.298
Just like it takes a village
to raise a child,

36:58.299 --> 37:01.427
it takes a village to save a single life.

37:15.358 --> 37:16.567
They'll be fine.

37:16.651 --> 37:18.569
The cooking steam means they'll survive.

37:23.324 --> 37:26.994
Don't be so obvious.
They might not like too much sympathy.

37:27.078 --> 37:30.539
So I shouldn't give these to them, then?
They're the hens' first laid eggs.

37:32.458 --> 37:35.127
Give them the eggs.
Pullet eggs will give them strength.

37:35.878 --> 37:37.296
These eggs are nothing.

37:37.964 --> 37:40.341
You're the one who gave away all our rice.

37:40.424 --> 37:42.969
You're the one
who gave them all our octopuses!

37:49.350 --> 37:50.893
So I was just wondering…

37:52.061 --> 37:53.145
I mean…

37:54.438 --> 37:55.731
Some rice--

37:55.815 --> 37:57.858
I don't understand what you're saying.

37:58.818 --> 38:00.236
Stop whining.

38:00.319 --> 38:02.280
There are many worse off than you.

38:10.621 --> 38:11.664
It was you, wasn't it?

38:13.040 --> 38:14.041
The rice jar.

38:15.334 --> 38:17.545
I don't know what you're talking about.

38:21.632 --> 38:23.676
What do you mean you don't know?

38:23.759 --> 38:25.177
I know you do.

38:25.803 --> 38:29.473
The rice jar was filling up,
not emptying out.

38:37.815 --> 38:40.651
I saw that the rice jar was empty
before I went to bed.

38:40.735 --> 38:42.320
I swear I saw it.

38:56.125 --> 38:59.628
Every morning, there was a little more,
then a little more.

39:01.047 --> 39:04.300
I thought I might not have seen it clearly
since it was nighttime.

39:04.383 --> 39:06.427
But it wasn't just for a day or two.

39:06.510 --> 39:09.472
There was always
just enough for a family of three.

39:09.555 --> 39:11.307
It just didn't make sense.

39:12.558 --> 39:14.060
Just enough to confuse me.

39:14.143 --> 39:16.187
It was the exact amount for three.

39:19.648 --> 39:20.733
Why do I bother?

39:21.567 --> 39:22.860
Why do I even bother?

39:27.198 --> 39:30.576
This isn't some magical jar,
and I'm not a fool.

39:30.659 --> 39:32.578
It also gave her a headache.

39:32.661 --> 39:35.915
If she had just given it to you,
you wouldn't have taken it.

39:35.998 --> 39:39.377
It gave her a headache,
trying to sneak you little bits at a time.

39:40.669 --> 39:42.338
If it was such a headache--

39:42.421 --> 39:46.133
Who would want to see
a pregnant woman go hungry?

39:49.720 --> 39:51.347
You go steam the octopus.

39:51.430 --> 39:53.099
I found it on my way home.

39:54.308 --> 39:57.269
Why do you keep taking care
of my mom's ancestral rites?

39:57.353 --> 40:00.689
If there's no octopus on your mom's table,
she'll scold you.

40:02.441 --> 40:05.152
Have you ever seen a haenyeo
diving on her own?

40:05.236 --> 40:09.532
When you're struggling to breathe
in the dark waters,

40:09.615 --> 40:13.494
you need to stay close to others
to survive.

40:13.577 --> 40:16.205
Or fear will grip your heart,
and you won't make it.

40:17.289 --> 40:19.125
No one can live on their own.

40:19.208 --> 40:21.127
Go together, with others.

40:21.210 --> 40:23.045
If you do, 100 miles will feel like ten.

40:23.129 --> 40:29.760
GO TOGETHER, WITH OTHERS.
IF YOU DO, 100 MILES WILL FEEL LIKE TEN.

40:35.474 --> 40:37.810
Gyeong-ja. That's Gwang-rye's daughter's.

40:39.728 --> 40:43.274
-Ae-sun is going to give birth soon.
-I'll give it to her.

40:43.357 --> 40:47.653
It's been a while,
so I just wanted to touch it.

40:48.362 --> 40:49.447
Right?

40:58.581 --> 41:01.041
Please write "Moral scholarship."

41:02.877 --> 41:05.754
If you write that, she'll understand.

41:12.803 --> 41:14.763
"Mo-ral."

41:14.847 --> 41:16.765
"Scholarship."

41:20.978 --> 41:21.812
Is this right?

41:23.606 --> 41:25.941
MO O-RAN SCHOLARSHIP
10,000 WON

41:28.444 --> 41:32.907
Is it wrong? Three months' rent
for the baby's family, right?

41:43.167 --> 41:44.627
Can you not read?

41:49.798 --> 41:51.342
One, two, three, four.

41:51.425 --> 41:53.135
One, ten, hundred, thousand.

41:55.471 --> 41:57.723
It's right. It's fine.

42:03.812 --> 42:04.647
Dear me.

42:05.147 --> 42:09.485
If only I hadn't hidden in that closet.

42:10.110 --> 42:11.904
Why did you pay their rent?

42:12.947 --> 42:16.909
I guess it's my fate
to live with wonder women.

42:18.327 --> 42:19.870
Don't you have any shame?

42:20.371 --> 42:23.832
Sure, I might deserve to be slapped
for what I've done.

42:24.333 --> 42:27.336
But you've done nothing wrong.
Love is not a sin, you know?

42:28.921 --> 42:30.714
Stop talking crap.

42:31.215 --> 42:33.509
Get your act together, okay?

42:34.093 --> 42:36.220
Karma is straightforward.

42:36.303 --> 42:39.890
Beasts raise beasts,
and nobility breeds nobility.

42:39.974 --> 42:43.727
Children perfectly inherit
their parents' traits.

42:43.811 --> 42:44.687
Min-ok,

42:45.271 --> 42:46.146
that's enough.

42:46.772 --> 42:48.232
She must have hated me.

42:49.233 --> 42:52.319
I ruined Oh Ae-sun's adolescence.

42:52.403 --> 42:55.906
I suppose I'm slyly trying to make up
for it with just 10,000 won.

42:55.990 --> 42:57.449
I gave her the cabbage field.

42:57.533 --> 42:59.952
That field of rocks?
That field of dog crap?

43:00.035 --> 43:03.038
It was Ae-sun's small hands
that plowed the entire field.

43:03.122 --> 43:07.293
And her mother owned that field
in the first place.

43:08.294 --> 43:09.295
Min-ok.

43:09.378 --> 43:11.547
You can run your mouth,
but have some decency.

43:11.630 --> 43:13.132
Quit talking rubbish.

43:13.215 --> 43:15.884
Min-ok, I told you to stop.
I can get mad too.

43:17.219 --> 43:18.804
Now that I've raised kids,

43:18.887 --> 43:23.892
I think even you, of all damn people,
should have paid for Ae-sun's college.

43:23.976 --> 43:27.187
Come on, that damn college. She can go!

43:28.314 --> 43:32.067
Tell her to go now. I'll pay for it,
even if I have to take out a loan.

43:32.151 --> 43:35.112
How could she go to college now? How?

43:35.195 --> 43:36.780
Just tell her to get into one!

43:36.864 --> 43:38.699
I'll lay down money before her!

43:39.742 --> 43:41.327
Say nothing if she doesn't get in.

43:41.827 --> 43:45.205
She doesn't need a degree to be a captain,
deputy chief, or whatever.

43:46.624 --> 43:48.876
She'll only get ripped off in Seoul.

43:49.668 --> 43:51.420
The best she'll get is a doctorate.

43:51.920 --> 43:54.006
She'll just bleed the family dry.

43:54.089 --> 43:57.801
Yes, the government office will hang
a congratulatory banner for her,

43:57.885 --> 43:59.720
but what's the point of all that?

44:02.389 --> 44:03.432
Geum-myeong.

44:07.603 --> 44:08.604
Hey, you're home.

44:13.317 --> 44:14.652
Did you get in?

44:15.319 --> 44:16.278
Did you not?

44:17.738 --> 44:18.572
Mom!

44:19.531 --> 44:21.784
If I didn't get in, who else could?

44:23.369 --> 44:24.745
Come on. Look at it.

44:24.828 --> 44:27.247
"Yang Geum-myeong."
It's got my name on it.

44:29.458 --> 44:30.292
Goodness me.

44:32.753 --> 44:34.421
Hey! Let's sell the boat!

44:37.800 --> 44:39.885
You did it, you did.

44:43.180 --> 44:46.392
I'm not sure
if it's okay for me to say this.

44:47.351 --> 44:52.523
I never thought I'd say this ever again.

44:53.399 --> 44:54.233
I'm…

44:54.316 --> 44:55.192
Are you happy?

44:57.986 --> 44:58.821
I am.

45:00.114 --> 45:00.948
Beyond words.

45:04.451 --> 45:05.786
I'm so happy!

45:08.706 --> 45:09.915
CERTIFICATE OF ADMISSION

45:09.998 --> 45:13.502
Okay. One, two, three.

45:18.006 --> 45:19.174
BOARDING HOUSE AVAILABLE

45:19.258 --> 45:20.384
AFFORDABLE ROOM FOR RENT

45:20.467 --> 45:21.802
RENT NEAR SNU
AFFORDABLE ROOM

45:24.763 --> 45:26.807
Geum-myeong!

45:38.610 --> 45:40.487
Is your child's name Geum-myeong?

45:41.363 --> 45:42.823
So is someone in our family.

45:44.867 --> 45:46.618
Your son's name is Geum-myeong?

45:46.702 --> 45:47.536
No.

45:48.120 --> 45:48.954
Mine is.

45:49.997 --> 45:50.998
I'm Geum-myeong.

45:52.040 --> 45:53.417
I'm Park Geum-myeong.

45:58.046 --> 45:59.298
Really?

45:59.381 --> 46:00.924
What an interesting coincidence.

46:01.008 --> 46:01.925
YALASHANG FILM CLUB

46:02.009 --> 46:03.218
What about jjajangmyeon?

46:03.302 --> 46:06.889
So, what's your major?

46:06.972 --> 46:08.474
Well, law is--

46:08.557 --> 46:11.810
Aren't we having jjajangmyeon?
Let's take the pictures and go.

46:11.894 --> 46:14.396
Let me take it
if you all want one together.

46:14.480 --> 46:16.064
That's so nice of you.

46:16.648 --> 46:18.901
Okay, you take ours, and I'll take yours.

46:18.984 --> 46:22.571
-Take whose picture? Why?
-Let's take it. Come on.

46:25.365 --> 46:26.658
Thank you.

46:28.535 --> 46:31.663
Here we go. One, two, three.

46:34.333 --> 46:35.584
I'll take one more.

46:39.171 --> 46:40.214
Smile.

46:42.007 --> 46:44.051
One, two, three!

46:46.011 --> 46:46.970
I didn't like him.

46:47.679 --> 46:50.140
I told you I didn't like that punk,
didn't I?

46:50.724 --> 46:51.767
What's wrong?

46:59.650 --> 47:01.485
When did Geum-myeong take a solo photo?

47:02.110 --> 47:05.280
That son of Park Geum-myeong
zoomed in on Geum-myeong.

47:05.364 --> 47:06.448
He zoomed in on her!

47:06.949 --> 47:08.325
I'll just take one more.

47:10.661 --> 47:11.578
Smile.

47:13.539 --> 47:15.415
One, two, three!

47:16.416 --> 47:18.335
So? Are you upset?

47:18.418 --> 47:20.712
-Call Geum-myeong right now.
-Why?

47:20.796 --> 47:22.714
You think they went to Busan together?

47:23.257 --> 47:24.883
Why would she go to Busan?

47:26.134 --> 47:29.972
You dragged someone else's daughter there,
but you won't let your daughter go?

47:30.055 --> 47:31.598
Did I drag you there?

47:32.224 --> 47:36.395
I think you'd be on the warpath
if she ever got married.

47:36.478 --> 47:38.063
Why would she get married?

47:46.864 --> 47:48.532
I'm letting you know now.

47:50.659 --> 47:51.869
I can't go tomorrow.

47:54.288 --> 47:55.163
Right.

47:56.248 --> 47:57.207
No need to come.

47:58.166 --> 47:59.042
You have a class.

48:01.503 --> 48:03.255
How can I go all the way to Nonsan?

48:04.089 --> 48:05.132
I can't.

48:07.175 --> 48:08.468
Go with your mom.

48:10.846 --> 48:11.722
It's fine.

48:12.890 --> 48:13.974
No need to come.

48:15.893 --> 48:17.394
Or go with Oh Ye-rim.

48:18.228 --> 48:19.479
Why would I go with her?

48:21.189 --> 48:23.817
Anyway, I can't go.

48:25.193 --> 48:26.278
I get it.

48:27.696 --> 48:29.489
I said I can't go!

48:29.573 --> 48:30.407
I said I got it.

48:30.490 --> 48:33.702
-Damn it, you don't get it.
-What is it now?

48:34.870 --> 48:36.705
What does it mean if I can't go?

48:39.333 --> 48:40.626
Tonight

48:41.668 --> 48:43.128
is our last night.

48:44.713 --> 48:47.132
Our last night before you join the army!

48:48.842 --> 48:50.385
Anyway, keep her in check.

48:51.386 --> 48:52.554
Your daughter…

48:52.638 --> 48:53.889
Do I really have to…

48:54.389 --> 48:55.807
What's wrong with you?

48:56.350 --> 48:58.518
…is just like you, Oh Ae-sun.

49:00.228 --> 49:03.523
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

49:07.069 --> 49:07.903
Sweetie.

49:15.744 --> 49:17.496
That's nice, isn't it?

49:18.580 --> 49:19.498
Yeah.

49:20.999 --> 49:23.752
Is it a lot more expensive
to live on higher floors?

49:25.837 --> 49:27.172
She said there was no room.

49:27.255 --> 49:28.548
You believe her?

49:29.675 --> 49:32.719
She can be a little short with us,
but she's still the eldest.

49:32.803 --> 49:36.431
And she always worries too much.
Even though I tell her not to.

49:36.515 --> 49:39.977
Why do people in Seoul build rooms
in the basement?

49:41.436 --> 49:45.107
It would break my heart
to see my baby live in the basement.

49:49.778 --> 49:52.990
Do you think anyone would buy
the cabbage field?

49:54.491 --> 49:55.575
Leave that one alone.

49:56.952 --> 49:57.869
But would they?

49:58.787 --> 50:00.372
Stop selling stuff.

50:01.665 --> 50:03.333
Why? You can't let it go?

50:04.334 --> 50:07.087
If we sell everything,
there'll be nothing left in your name.

50:07.587 --> 50:10.007
Whatever. Your wife over your daughter?

50:13.552 --> 50:15.554
You know, looking back,

50:16.263 --> 50:17.764
those days were nice.

50:18.932 --> 50:21.018
Was that the summer of our lives?

50:22.853 --> 50:24.771
Everything was so new back then.

50:25.564 --> 50:28.108
Everything felt awkward and difficult,

50:28.191 --> 50:30.110
but it was all a first.

50:31.236 --> 50:33.155
I loved everything.

50:42.873 --> 50:43.999
First love,

50:45.375 --> 50:46.460
our first night…

50:48.587 --> 50:49.755
our first home,

50:50.338 --> 50:53.216
our first boat, our first full net.

50:54.301 --> 50:55.302
Our first child.

50:56.678 --> 50:58.221
Having our first child…

50:59.890 --> 51:01.308
No words can describe it.

51:04.811 --> 51:06.855
Still, leave the cabbage field.

51:18.408 --> 51:20.535
Just leave the cabbage field.

51:21.369 --> 51:25.665
That field is your reward
for surviving that summer.

51:26.958 --> 51:30.212
I wondered how we could move forward.

51:32.255 --> 51:34.633
But life really did go on.

51:36.843 --> 51:38.804
Life went on and on.

51:39.888 --> 51:42.808
LIFE GOES ON AND ON

54:33.228 --> 54:37.816
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOS
WILL FLOW AND FLOW UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."

54:44.781 --> 54:46.908
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
